    "text": "allwny.com\nwebsite\nJamestown\nRochester and Jamestown man charged for alleged roles in narcotics conspiracy\nBy All WNY News,\n1 days agoBUFFALO — U.S. Attorney Michael DiGiacomo announced today a federal grand jury returned an indictment charging Johnny B. Mays aka Blaze, 40, of Rochester and Jamestown, NY, with conspiracy to possess with intent to distribute, and to distribute, one kilogram or more heroin, 400 grams or more of fentanyl, and five kilograms or more of cocaine, which carries a mandatory minimum penalty of 10 years in prison and a maximum of life.",
